{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/842743-conspiracy-conspiracy-theories","id":842743,"title":"Conspiracy Conspiracy Theories","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-05T15:16:42-08:00","id":842743,"title":"Conspiracy Conspiracy Theories","content":"So, it goes without saying that the Conspiracies all have secrets. Some have been revealed to us, others have been left up to our imagination. I figured it would be fun to see what fan theories people have cooked up to fill in the blanks, or just to add depth to these shadowy organizations. These don't just have to be about the Conspiracies, either; wild speculation regarding Compacts is fine too.<br /> <br /> So here's one that just recently hit me and inspired me to start this thread:<br /> <br /> <b>The Aegis Kai Doru <i>are</i> the Daughters of Nibiru</b><br /> <br /> Well, the Inner Circle are, at least. True, they're not all women, but the recruiting policies of the conspiracy may have changed somewhat over the last six thousand years or so. Just think about it: there are nine of them, all of whom belong to a ancient bloodlines with mythic (and possibly falsified) origins. It's been suggested that the Nibiru recruited along family lines, and had Endowments that at least partly resembled those of the Aegis Kai Doru.<br /> <br /> If the &quot;Simon Romance&quot; is to be believed, the Nibiru existed into at least the 1st century AD, before ultimately mysteriously disappearing. The most obvious hypothesis, of course, is that they simply died out. No family in the world can reliably trace its heritage back so many thousands of years, and the Nibiru certainly had many enemies who wanted them gone. And perhaps they <i>were</i> dying out, and were forced to re-invent themselves to survive, like a fugitive changing his name and appearance.<br /> <br /> In place of ancient Sumerian poems forgotten by the world, they adopted the language and mythology of the Hellenistic culture that was, at the time, dominant in the eastern Mediterranean. In place of a mad sorcerer-king from the dawn of history, the Nibiru concocted a new origin story for themselves, cobbling it together from the secret legends told by the very enemies with whom they had struggled for so many generations. Being oriented around an antediluvian struggle between good and evil and a subsequent fall from grace had the added benefit of making their new mythology more familiar to the various factions of Christians that were rapidly spreading across the Greek-speaking world at the time.<br /> <br /> If we accept this theory, the question becomes this: does the current incarnation of the Inner Circle even remember their true origins? I think that at least some of them might.<br /> <br /> See, although they collect artifacts of all kinds, the Aegis Kai Doru seems to have a particular interest in magical severed heads. Perhaps this is because the Daughters of Nibiru are still searching for something they lost a long time ago; three things, actually. One of them sings laments in a secret vault under Marrakesh, but the two remaining heads of the eldest Daughters remain beyond the grasp of the conspiracy. Perhaps the inner circle is searching for a way to finally give their earliest foremothers peace by freeing them from their accursed half-life. Perhaps they're seeking magical secrets that have been forgotten since the days of the first generation of Daughters. Maybe they just want to cover up all the information they can about the Nibiru, to prevent people from asking questions about what became of the ancient conspiracy. In any case, they continue to issue orders for their agents to look into rumors of strange, disembodied heads the world over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 03-05-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}